[h1]Meals at Work[/h1]
When pawns get hungry while crafting or researching, they order a meal. Haulers bring food to them so they can eat at their workstation and save the trip to the dining room.

[h2]Make room for lunch[/h2]
[list]
[*]Automatic meal delivery: workers place orders when a courier is available, with food chosen according to each recipient's diet.
[*]Several meals per trip: couriers collect food for multiple orders and deliver them in one round.
[*]Eat while working: enjoy the delivered meal at the workstation and keep crafting or researching at a slightly slower pace.
[*]Take a lunch break: crafters can step away for a meal and return to finish their work.
[*]Make use of spare space: idle worktables double as dining spots, with distance and a preference for dining tables guiding the choice.
[*]Make it your own: customize the small workstation dining mood effect, meal preferences and delivery waiting time.
[/list]

[h2]A team effort[/h2]
Colonists, mechs with hauling work and animals trained to haul can deliver meals. Player mechs with a food need can enjoy meals at work too.
Supports RimWorld 1.6; requires Harmony. Includes compatibility for Common Sense, Pick Up And Haul and Schedule Everything, plus Simplified Chinese localization.

